Calc: a formula naming what Calc lacks keeps the file's result

- XLSX and ODS import mark a formula cell holding an unknown name
  (ocBad) and a loaded result: its result stands, through the hard
  recalc on load too, so its dependents use it and a save writes it
  back (Ely #D-02; PRD §288). A changed input (Notify) or SetDirty
  (an edit, a reference update) ends that; it then recalcs to #NAME?.
- An unknown function keeps its spelling instead of being lowercased,
  so the formula written back names it as read.
- .uno:KeptResults lists such cells with their sheet.

